-- #1383 face 1 — THE DRAIN CELL for the S1 this issue filed, and the layout half of
-- it that no fixture could express before.
--
-- A named-field-variant CONSTRUCTOR (`Plain`, one of `Holder`'s variants, in ahold)
-- collides by BARE NAME with an unrelated module's record TYPE (plainlib's `Plain`).
-- `mkH.hx` is a projection of ahold's declaration and has nothing to do with
-- plainlib; before Q-IDENT it was REJECTED at exit 1 with `Type mismatch: Holder vs
-- Plain` plus `Field 'hx' does not belong to record 'Plain'` — a diagnostic naming a
-- type this program never puts in that position.
--
-- WHY THE FALLBACK IS REACHED AT ALL (so a future edit does not silently defuse it):
-- `mkH`'s head is `Holder` but its registry key is `Plain`, so `resolveFieldRecord`'s
-- exact `lookupRecordByName "Holder"` misses, the identity companion has no row under
-- `Holder`, and no key suffix-matches `__Holder`.  Control lands in
-- `resolveFieldByOwners`, which answered `pairRecordByName` — the ONE row the bare key
-- `Plain` currently reaches, decided by module registration order.  Rewrite `ahold` as
-- a short-form record and this cell silently stops testing anything.
--
-- ⚠️ THE OWNER SET WAS NEVER THE DEFECT.  `fieldOwnerNames "hx"` is the SINGLETON
-- `["Plain"]` here — the RIGHT key — and it is `sortUniqS`ed, so `headL` is
-- order-insensitive.  What was wrong is which DECLARATION that one key reached.  A
-- narrowing/reachability analysis over the owner set would not have moved this cell.
--
-- Expected output, derived BY HAND from the sources before anything was run and
-- independently of any engine:
--   ahold:    mkH = Plain { hx = 100, hy = 200 }  =>  mkH.hx = 100, mkH.hy = 200
--   plainlib: mkP = Plain { hy = 7,   hx = 5 }    =>  mkP.hx = 5,   mkP.hy = 7
-- so `h=100,200 p=5,7`.
--
-- ⚠️ THE FIELD ORDERS ARE OPPOSITE ON PURPOSE.  If the selection regressed to picking
-- plainlib's record for `mkH.hx` the front end rejects (loud); if some future change
-- made it ACCEPT with the wrong record, the projection would read plainlib's slot 1
-- for `hx` and this cell reds on the VALUE.  Both failure directions are covered, and
-- the second is the one `record_receiver_ident_*`'s single-field ancestors could not
-- see.
--
-- ⚠️ `mkP.hx`/`mkP.hy` are NOT redundant with the ahold half.  They take a DIFFERENT
-- path — a plain record's head IS its key, so `resolveFieldRecord` arm (a) answers
-- them out of the identity companion (#1319 unit 3), never reaching the fallback this
-- cell is about.  They are the "unrelated code still behaves" half.
import ahold.{Holder, mkH}
import plainlib.{Plain, mkP}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  putStrLn
    ("h=" ++ intToString mkH.hx ++ "," ++ intToString mkH.hy ++ " p=" ++ intToString mkP.hx ++ "," ++ intToString mkP.hy)
